1
00:00:00,092 --> 00:00:03,765
Loupe now keeps the places you shoot as well as the photographs.

2
00:00:04,079 --> 00:00:07,697
This recording drives the real Angular application against the real

3
00:00:07,697 --> 00:00:12,224
API, worker, and database, with a local embedding model running

4
00:00:12,224 --> 00:00:13,094
beside them.

5
00:00:13,408 --> 00:00:16,844
It starts by signing in with a locally provisioned account.

6
00:00:18,452 --> 00:00:22,768
Locations opens on the whole library: seven places, each a

7
00:00:22,768 --> 00:00:26,440
card with its cover, name, locality, and image count.

8
00:00:26,755 --> 00:00:30,715
Hovering a card reveals those details, and every card carries its

9
00:00:30,715 --> 00:00:34,598
report status; none of these has a scouting report yet.

10
00:00:34,899 --> 00:00:37,059
Find a location sits in the header.

11
00:00:38,652 --> 00:00:43,588
Adding a location is one dialog: a name, an address you type yourself,

12
00:00:43,757 --> 00:00:48,021
never read from a photo, a setting, a scouting brief, private notes,

13
00:00:48,021 --> 00:00:48,943
and tags.

14
00:00:49,244 --> 00:00:52,915
Save, and the new card appears at the front of the library with a

15
00:00:52,915 --> 00:00:55,377
placeholder until it has images.

16
00:00:56,972 --> 00:00:59,368
A location holds up to ten images.

17
00:00:59,656 --> 00:01:03,275
Choose several at once and each one uploads on its own with its own

18
00:01:03,275 --> 00:01:04,184
progress.

19
00:01:04,498 --> 00:01:08,592
The gallery shows the full frame, the thumbnails are a radio group,

20
00:01:08,788 --> 00:01:12,591
so the arrow keys move the selection, and any image can become the

21
00:01:12,591 --> 00:01:13,197
cover.

22
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:19,011
The brief, notes, and tags save inline, each with its own status.

23
00:01:19,312 --> 00:01:23,667
Every save records an index intent: the status reads Updating

24
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:27,195
search while the worker embeds the location through the local model,

25
00:01:27,575 --> 00:01:29,998
and clears the moment the vector is current.

26
00:01:31,572 --> 00:01:35,638
A scouting report is requested explicitly, and the disclosure says

27
00:01:35,638 --> 00:01:39,835
exactly what leaves the server: the images, the brief, and camera

28
00:01:39,835 --> 00:01:43,929
settings; never the address, coordinates, notes, or tags.

29
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:48,730
This stack has no Azure OpenAI credentials, so the request is refused

30
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:51,692
with a clear message, and editing continues.

31
00:01:53,292 --> 00:01:57,239
What a finished report looks like is on the design-system site, with

32
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,609
synthetic content.

33
00:01:58,911 --> 00:02:03,529
Six sections in a fixed order: overview, suitability by shoot type,

34
00:02:03,529 --> 00:02:06,886
times of day, techniques, group size, and cautions.

35
00:02:07,187 --> 00:02:11,715
Ratings are words, never scores, every entry names its evidence basis,

36
00:02:11,897 --> 00:02:14,517
and citing an image selects it in the gallery.

37
00:02:16,132 --> 00:02:18,871
Find a location searches your own library.

38
00:02:19,172 --> 00:02:23,329
Keyword mode matches every word you type against a location's details

39
00:02:23,329 --> 00:02:25,792
and, once it has one, its report.

40
00:02:26,093 --> 00:02:30,527
Setting and tag filters work on any location, including the one added

41
00:02:30,527 --> 00:02:35,568
a moment ago, while shoot type, people, and time of day read the report.

42
00:02:37,172 --> 00:02:41,185
Meaning mode ranks by what the locations describe, not by matching

43
00:02:41,185 --> 00:02:41,871
words.

44
00:02:42,198 --> 00:02:46,238
The query is embedded by the local model and compared with each location's

45
00:02:46,238 --> 00:02:50,240
current vector, and the results carry the Matched by meaning label.

46
00:02:50,567 --> 00:02:54,646
A calm waterside shoot at first light surfaces the water locations

47
00:02:54,646 --> 00:02:57,424
first, without those words in their tags.

48
00:02:59,025 --> 00:03:03,341
Everything shown was saved for real: the location, its images and

49
00:03:03,341 --> 00:03:07,262
cover, the notes, the tags, and every search index update are in the

50
00:03:07,262 --> 00:03:10,645
database, and both searches found them a moment later.

51
00:03:10,959 --> 00:03:15,790
That is the Locations area today: keep the places, ask for the report,

52
00:03:15,959 --> 00:03:17,816
and find the right one for the shoot.
